WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.152 --> 00:00:02.485
(whooshing)

00:00:03.396 --> 00:00:04.229
- Focused.

00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:05.062
- Focus.

00:00:05.062 --> 00:00:05.895
- Stay focused.

00:00:05.895 --> 00:00:06.728
- Your focus.

00:00:06.728 --> 00:00:07.561
- Focused.

00:00:07.561 --> 00:00:08.394
- Focus.

00:00:08.394 --> 00:00:09.227
- Focus.

00:00:09.227 --> 00:00:10.060
- Stay focused.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.325
- Hello believe nation, my
name is Evan Charmichael,

00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:14.318
my one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:14.318 --> 00:00:17.844
are going to solve all of
the world's major problems.

00:00:17.844 --> 00:00:20.264
So to help you on your journey
today we're going to talk about

00:00:20.264 --> 00:00:22.869
how you can be focused.

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:24.883
And as always, as you're
watching if you hear something

00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:26.911
that really resonates
with you, please leave it

00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:28.721
down in the comments below
and put quotes around it

00:00:28.721 --> 00:00:32.073
so other people can be inspired,
and when you write it down

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:35.355
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself, as well.

00:00:35.355 --> 00:00:36.763
Enjoy.

00:00:36.763 --> 00:00:39.930
(inspirational music)

00:00:47.804 --> 00:00:50.470
- Everyone in this room
knows how to create.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.634
You're not a manager of your life,

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.005
you're a creator of your life

00:00:54.005 --> 00:00:56.790
or you wouldn't be in this room.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.003
How do you create your life?

00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:02.527
You get hungry for something, don't you?

00:01:02.527 --> 00:01:05.097
Who has done something in
your life that once seemed

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:08.400
difficult or impossible and
now it's part of your life?

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.607
Who's got something in your
life in this area, say aye.

00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:11.528
- [Audience] Aye.

00:01:11.528 --> 00:01:12.777
- How did you do it?

00:01:12.777 --> 00:01:14.328
You created it three ways.

00:01:14.328 --> 00:01:17.898
Number one, you decided there's
something you wanted so bad

00:01:17.898 --> 00:01:19.959
that you unleashed all your desire.

00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:21.825
You became obsessed with it.

00:01:21.825 --> 00:01:24.476
If it was a business, or
a car, or a relationship,

00:01:24.476 --> 00:01:27.426
or a transformation in your body,

00:01:27.426 --> 00:01:30.106
if there's something you once
envisioned and now it's real

00:01:30.106 --> 00:01:31.935
it's cause you didn't just envision it,

00:01:31.935 --> 00:01:34.107
you brought so much emotion to it

00:01:34.107 --> 00:01:37.206
that now it's in your
life, it was once a dream,

00:01:37.206 --> 00:01:40.067
it was once a goal, and
now it's in your life.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.321
How many have something
like that in your lives now,

00:01:42.321 --> 00:01:43.197
say aye.

00:01:43.197 --> 00:01:45.389
- [Audience] Aye.

00:01:45.389 --> 00:01:48.371
- You may take it for granted now,

00:01:48.371 --> 00:01:50.050
hopefully not,

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.809
but it was once just a vision.

00:01:51.809 --> 00:01:53.915
It may have seemed impossible at one time,

00:01:53.915 --> 00:01:55.507
so how did you do it?

00:01:55.507 --> 00:01:58.353
You started with a concrete
vision of what you wanted

00:01:58.353 --> 00:02:01.878
and you focused on it
continuously, didn't you?

00:02:01.878 --> 00:02:04.319
Wherever focus goes, energy.

00:02:04.319 --> 00:02:05.152
- [Audience] Flows.

00:02:05.152 --> 00:02:05.985
- Flows.

00:02:06.998 --> 00:02:08.899
You envisioned something,
you got clear about it,

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:10.838
and then you started thinking
about all the reasons

00:02:10.838 --> 00:02:12.626
why you wanted it.

00:02:12.626 --> 00:02:14.588
You got excited about it.

00:02:14.588 --> 00:02:17.168
Said this is what's next for me now.

00:02:17.168 --> 00:02:18.666
I want this.

00:02:18.666 --> 00:02:20.297
You may have dreamed about
it, thought about it,

00:02:20.297 --> 00:02:22.304
talked about it, but when you focus

00:02:22.304 --> 00:02:25.266
on something continuously
something magical happens.

00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:27.127
You get insights, don't you?

00:02:27.127 --> 00:02:29.097
You overhear a conversation
and you hear something

00:02:29.097 --> 00:02:30.699
you wouldn't have heard
if you didn't have that

00:02:30.699 --> 00:02:34.040
outcome or goal that you wanted so badly.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.501
Who's ever come up with
something, obsessed about it,

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:39.247
didn't even know how to do
it, and it just happened,

00:02:39.247 --> 00:02:41.705
and it came together, who's
had that experience, say aye.

00:02:41.705 --> 00:02:42.538
- [Audience] Aye.

00:02:42.538 --> 00:02:44.042
- So why don't we tap into that power now

00:02:44.042 --> 00:02:45.697
for your business and life.

00:02:45.697 --> 00:02:49.575
- I realized that to
have the level of success

00:02:49.575 --> 00:02:52.988
that I want to have, it's
difficult to spread it out

00:02:52.988 --> 00:02:54.828
and do multiple things,

00:02:54.828 --> 00:02:57.078
in order to be world class,

00:02:58.603 --> 00:03:01.574
and I made a decision, I
want to be world class.

00:03:01.574 --> 00:03:05.324
And it takes such a
desperate obsessive focus

00:03:07.104 --> 00:03:09.068
to excel on a level that

00:03:09.068 --> 00:03:10.735
I want to make movies.

00:03:11.684 --> 00:03:14.192
You know, Star Wars, when I was young,

00:03:14.192 --> 00:03:16.219
I sat in a movie theater
and watched Star Wars

00:03:16.219 --> 00:03:19.372
and I just couldn't believe
that that movie made me

00:03:19.372 --> 00:03:22.002
feel like that, just
floored and just stunned

00:03:22.002 --> 00:03:23.506
by the creativity.

00:03:23.506 --> 00:03:27.051
And just I'm realizing that
in order to move people

00:03:27.051 --> 00:03:29.827
in that way, in order to
touch people in that way,

00:03:29.827 --> 00:03:32.645
you really got to focus
with all of your fiber,

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.927
and all of your heart, and
all of your creativity.

00:03:34.927 --> 00:03:36.213
- You want to make your dream come true,

00:03:36.213 --> 00:03:37.406
you got to stay focused.

00:03:37.406 --> 00:03:39.193
Some people rather get
even than get ahead,

00:03:39.193 --> 00:03:41.664
stay focused on where you want to go.

00:03:41.664 --> 00:03:44.450
I just kept on doing what
I was supposed to do.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.914
And so I was driving to the radio station,

00:03:46.914 --> 00:03:49.331
my opponent had over $20,000,

00:03:50.544 --> 00:03:53.077
I had less than $800.

00:03:53.077 --> 00:03:55.072
As I was in the radio
station, the guy said,

00:03:55.072 --> 00:03:57.130
you're going to make a
commercial, I said yes.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.956
He said, it better be a
good one because that money

00:03:58.956 --> 00:04:00.508
can't go pretty far here.

00:04:00.508 --> 00:04:02.649
(audience laughs)

00:04:02.649 --> 00:04:04.487
And I sat there in the middle control room

00:04:04.487 --> 00:04:06.234
and I was thinking.

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:09.632
And here's what happens
when you get still.

00:04:09.632 --> 00:04:11.253
Stuff will start coming.

00:04:11.253 --> 00:04:14.031
Something said, call your
mom, you use to talk about

00:04:14.031 --> 00:04:15.709
your mother on the air all the time,

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:17.756
ask her to say a few words for you,

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:20.045
that'll be a different
kind of political spot.

00:04:20.045 --> 00:04:21.539
(audience laughs)

00:04:21.539 --> 00:04:25.304
So I called my mom and I
had a gospel record playing

00:04:25.304 --> 00:04:26.698
in the background.

00:04:26.698 --> 00:04:30.615
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:04:33.964 --> 00:04:37.554
And then I had my mother say,
hello, this is Mrs. Brown,

00:04:37.554 --> 00:04:41.197
when I raised my sons I raised
them to be good children,

00:04:41.197 --> 00:04:43.196
when they got out of
hand I beat their behind

00:04:43.196 --> 00:04:44.543
and made them go right,

00:04:44.543 --> 00:04:47.228
please vote for my son, he's a good boy.

00:04:47.228 --> 00:04:51.145
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:04:55.589 --> 00:04:57.271
Usually in a state representative race

00:04:57.271 --> 00:04:59.516
maybe three or four thousand
people will come out

00:04:59.516 --> 00:05:01.197
to vote in a primary.

00:05:01.197 --> 00:05:04.286
And that primary race over 27,000 people

00:05:04.286 --> 00:05:06.500
came out and voted and said,
I'm voting for Les Brown

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.085
cause his mother say
he's a good boy. (laughs)

00:05:09.085 --> 00:05:11.447
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:05:11.447 --> 00:05:13.451
I won, ladies and gentlemen.

00:05:13.451 --> 00:05:14.829
I won.

00:05:14.829 --> 00:05:17.829
(audience applauds)

00:05:22.842 --> 00:05:25.031
So you've got to be
willing to stay focused,

00:05:25.031 --> 00:05:27.240
to be creative, to be relentless,

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.973
because things are going to happen to you

00:05:28.973 --> 00:05:30.638
when you're working on your dream.

00:05:30.638 --> 00:05:33.798
- What kinds of business
ideas have you said no to?

00:05:33.798 --> 00:05:35.965
- I'm saying no to a lot of ideas

00:05:35.965 --> 00:05:39.290
because as a CEO I have to
say no to opportunities,

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:42.402
because if I say yes, I
probably get 5,000 opportunities

00:05:42.402 --> 00:05:46.709
every day, but whether yes
or no, everything based on

00:05:46.709 --> 00:05:50.420
the mission that we're
helping doing business easier,

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.320
it's on that we will consider.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.830
If somebody come and
say, can you, we will,

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.752
you know, have business deal,
we'll make a lot of money,

00:05:56.752 --> 00:05:57.870
I'm not interested.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.724
- It's easy to discard,
say, 10 terrible ideas

00:06:01.724 --> 00:06:03.518
and go after the one good idea,

00:06:03.518 --> 00:06:06.703
but when you start to get
a little bit of momentum

00:06:06.703 --> 00:06:09.990
you can drown yourself
in good opportunities

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.571
that aren't great opportunities.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.575
And if you scatter your
focus, you try to do

00:06:13.575 --> 00:06:17.260
17 different product lines,
you can kill your business

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:20.474
really easily, particularly
when you have a small team.

00:06:20.474 --> 00:06:23.780
So I think asking yourself
repeatedly, what is the one

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.252
project, the one initiative,
the one campaign that

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:29.946
if successful will render
the rest of these things

00:06:29.946 --> 00:06:33.236
either unnecessary or much, much easier,

00:06:33.236 --> 00:06:35.836
what is that one step?

00:06:35.836 --> 00:06:38.146
And I've called it this
dead domino before,

00:06:38.146 --> 00:06:40.919
but what is the one thing on
this list of seven different

00:06:40.919 --> 00:06:42.665
campaigns that will
make all the other ones

00:06:42.665 --> 00:06:44.659
irrelevant or much easier?

00:06:44.659 --> 00:06:47.302
- How do you, I mean, that's
a tough answer, isn't it?

00:06:47.302 --> 00:06:49.323
Because they all sound good.

00:06:49.323 --> 00:06:51.887
- Yeah, I think they can,

00:06:51.887 --> 00:06:55.683
and I think that what it
comes down to often times is,

00:06:55.683 --> 00:06:58.126
it returns back to
measurements, so how are we

00:06:58.126 --> 00:07:00.876
defining success, like if
we want to grow the company,

00:07:00.876 --> 00:07:02.642
let's just say, what does that mean,

00:07:02.642 --> 00:07:05.324
in three months, six months,
what are we measuring,

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:07.599
why are we measuring those things,

00:07:07.599 --> 00:07:10.766
and what is a, sort of a comfort goal,

00:07:11.846 --> 00:07:14.705
meaning like, okay, we think
we can easily hit this number,

00:07:14.705 --> 00:07:17.597
what is a stretch, and what is like,

00:07:17.597 --> 00:07:19.977
hallelujah, we threaded our needle,

00:07:19.977 --> 00:07:24.158
and then come up with a really
concrete number to tackle,

00:07:24.158 --> 00:07:26.301
and once you have that
number then you can look

00:07:26.301 --> 00:07:27.783
at those five and say,
alright, which of those

00:07:27.783 --> 00:07:29.440
are going to serve us right now.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.523
And I'm dealing with that increasingly so

00:07:32.523 --> 00:07:36.227
because out of all these
different branches of content,

00:07:36.227 --> 00:07:38.474
and activities, and angel
investing, and so on,

00:07:38.474 --> 00:07:40.284
it's very easy for me to get scattered,

00:07:40.284 --> 00:07:42.254
it's never been easier,
so I have to continually

00:07:42.254 --> 00:07:43.340
ask that type of question.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.789
- What's your main focus now,

00:07:44.789 --> 00:07:47.372
if you had to boil it down to one?

00:07:47.372 --> 00:07:49.705
- My main focus right now is

00:07:50.576 --> 00:07:54.843
building my podcast, Tim Ferriss
Show, up to a point where

00:07:54.843 --> 00:07:58.483
it's consistently in the top
10 to 15 on iTunes so that

00:07:58.483 --> 00:08:01.115
I can establish a presence
and name recognition

00:08:01.115 --> 00:08:03.288
in Hollywood and entertainment,
which I can leverage then

00:08:03.288 --> 00:08:06.858
for the TV show and film
projects that I'll be

00:08:06.858 --> 00:08:09.218
expanding into in the
next three to nine months.

00:08:09.218 --> 00:08:13.757
And specifically what that
means is targeted advertising,

00:08:13.757 --> 00:08:17.692
for the podcast, specifically
towards people who are

00:08:17.692 --> 00:08:20.379
producers, agents, actors, directors,

00:08:20.379 --> 00:08:22.039
in Hollywood and New York City,

00:08:22.039 --> 00:08:23.655
all of that can be quantified.

00:08:23.655 --> 00:08:26.703
- The one thing that I feel deeply about,

00:08:26.703 --> 00:08:28.857
and this is something
I'll feel deeply about

00:08:28.857 --> 00:08:31.024
when I leave government is

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:36.011
stuff gets better if we work at it

00:08:36.011 --> 00:08:39.215
and we stay focused on where we're going.

00:08:39.215 --> 00:08:42.543
It doesn't immediately get all solved,

00:08:42.543 --> 00:08:44.879
and I warned against this
when I was running for office

00:08:44.879 --> 00:08:46.826
because everybody had the Hope posters,

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:48.150
and the this, and the that, and everybody

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:49.391
was feeling like, man.

00:08:49.391 --> 00:08:50.486
- Hey, we didn't make
those, you made those.

00:08:50.486 --> 00:08:52.543
(audience laughs)
Quit blaming us.

00:08:52.543 --> 00:08:54.165
- No, no, no, no, no.
- That wasn't us, was it?

00:08:54.165 --> 00:08:55.624
- Hold on a second, no, no,

00:08:55.624 --> 00:08:57.657
no, I like the poster.

00:08:57.657 --> 00:08:58.824
- I'm pretty sure that came from you.

00:08:58.824 --> 00:09:00.123
- It was a nice poster.

00:09:00.123 --> 00:09:02.141
No, but what I'm saying is is that

00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:04.923
if you look at what I
said at the time, I said,

00:09:04.923 --> 00:09:07.580
this is going to be an ongoing project,

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.524
and it's a project of citizens.

00:09:09.524 --> 00:09:11.357
It's not just, fix it.

00:09:12.396 --> 00:09:16.396
It's how do we work
together to get things done,

00:09:17.264 --> 00:09:22.216
and it will be imperfect,
but over time is it better?

00:09:22.216 --> 00:09:23.926
And here's the thing I can say, John,

00:09:23.926 --> 00:09:26.700
I can say this unequivocally,

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.680
the VA is better now than
when I came into office,

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.189
it is better now than
when I came into office.

00:09:32.189 --> 00:09:34.932
Government works better than
when I came into office.

00:09:34.932 --> 00:09:38.051
The economy, by every metric, is better

00:09:38.051 --> 00:09:39.581
than when I came into office.

00:09:39.581 --> 00:09:43.863
And so the reason I can sleep
at night is I say to myself,

00:09:43.863 --> 00:09:45.299
(audience applauds)
you know what, it's better.

00:09:45.299 --> 00:09:48.289
Now, am I satisfied with it, no.

00:09:48.289 --> 00:09:49.861
And should voters be satisfied with it?

00:09:49.861 --> 00:09:53.260
Absolutely not because
otherwise if we get complacent

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:56.234
and lazy then stuff doesn't happen.

00:09:56.234 --> 00:10:00.401
- Losing focus is another way
that founders get off track.

00:10:01.263 --> 00:10:04.079
I actually think this
is a symptom of burnout.

00:10:04.079 --> 00:10:05.921
When you get really burned
out on running the business

00:10:05.921 --> 00:10:07.184
you want to do easier things,

00:10:07.184 --> 00:10:09.330
or sort of more gratifying things.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:12.170
You want to go to
conferences and have people

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.714
tell you how great you are.

00:10:13.714 --> 00:10:15.228
You want to do all these
things that are not actually

00:10:15.228 --> 00:10:17.927
building the business, and

00:10:17.927 --> 00:10:21.379
the most common post YC
failure case for the companies

00:10:21.379 --> 00:10:23.810
we fund is that they're incredibly focused

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.315
during a YC on their
company, and then after

00:10:26.315 --> 00:10:28.097
they start doing a lot of other things.

00:10:28.097 --> 00:10:33.047
They advise companies, they
go to conferences, whatever.

00:10:33.047 --> 00:10:36.008
Focus is what made you
successful in the first place.

00:10:36.008 --> 00:10:38.241
There are a lot of
reasons people lose focus,

00:10:38.241 --> 00:10:40.262
but fight against that
really, really hard.

00:10:40.262 --> 00:10:41.755
- But the reason I made
it is because I knew

00:10:41.755 --> 00:10:43.686
exactly what I wanted to do,
see that's the thing I see

00:10:43.686 --> 00:10:45.822
with a lot of people
nowadays, they be confused,

00:10:45.822 --> 00:10:49.032
like they don't really
have a clear cut, concise

00:10:49.032 --> 00:10:51.557
goal in mind, or they
don't have that one thing

00:10:51.557 --> 00:10:52.976
that they feel that they're good at,

00:10:52.976 --> 00:10:54.189
so they don't try to master it.

00:10:54.189 --> 00:10:55.456
Like I'm reading a book right now called

00:10:55.456 --> 00:10:57.972
The Mastery by Robert Greene,
and it's basically taking

00:10:57.972 --> 00:11:00.639
that whole 10,000 hour theory,
like you're not a master

00:11:00.639 --> 00:11:03.029
in something until you've
put in 10,000 hours in it.

00:11:03.029 --> 00:11:03.974
- Practice worth 10,000 hours.

00:11:03.974 --> 00:11:06.627
- Yeah, so it's like you
got to find that one thing

00:11:06.627 --> 00:11:08.559
to put in that time
with, and everything else

00:11:08.559 --> 00:11:11.448
will sprout from it, like
radio was my thing, then I'm.

00:11:11.448 --> 00:11:13.081
- So what you're saying is that
you always knew then radio,

00:11:13.081 --> 00:11:14.188
like once it clicked.
- Always, man.

00:11:14.188 --> 00:11:16.688
- I don't know, you know, I've

00:11:18.031 --> 00:11:22.121
tried to keep my focus on
the music that I was making.

00:11:22.121 --> 00:11:25.096
I tried not to get distracted.

00:11:25.096 --> 00:11:26.263
I had a lot of

00:11:27.367 --> 00:11:29.597
models who came before
me where I could see

00:11:29.597 --> 00:11:32.725
where people made mistakes,
and nobody's perfect,

00:11:32.725 --> 00:11:35.475
you make mistakes, you know, and,

00:11:36.567 --> 00:11:39.720
you know, it's just a part of

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.137
human life, but I think that,

00:11:43.176 --> 00:11:46.719
that the kind of mistakes
where you lose your center

00:11:46.719 --> 00:11:49.537
and you lose track of the
work that you're doing

00:11:49.537 --> 00:11:52.428
and the music you're making, and you lose,

00:11:52.428 --> 00:11:56.412
you lose the ability to
be relevant to your fans,

00:11:56.412 --> 00:12:00.162
and to the community
that you're working for.

00:12:02.018 --> 00:12:04.083
I've just done my best
with them, you know,

00:12:04.083 --> 00:12:07.215
I'd be the last person to claim any,

00:12:07.215 --> 00:12:11.382
make any claim on getting it
completely right or perfect,

00:12:12.885 --> 00:12:16.552
but I've tried to do
it well enough to where

00:12:18.108 --> 00:12:21.024
I continue to have a voice for my fans

00:12:21.024 --> 00:12:23.032
and I'm able to look into the world

00:12:23.032 --> 00:12:26.282
and experience and translate what I see

00:12:27.713 --> 00:12:30.143
in a productive fashion.

00:12:30.143 --> 00:12:32.373
- Well, when you're doing
a TV show, you know,

00:12:32.373 --> 00:12:34.499
every day is a different
day in the sense that

00:12:34.499 --> 00:12:37.604
it's never the same, and you
might be shooting two scenes,

00:12:37.604 --> 00:12:40.413
you might have one scene,
you might have five scenes.

00:12:40.413 --> 00:12:44.580
So your level of preparation
is different every time.

00:12:46.034 --> 00:12:48.928
Generally, I'm up early,
I exercise, I run,

00:12:48.928 --> 00:12:50.828
I do whatever it is that I'm doing

00:12:50.828 --> 00:12:53.157
in terms of my physical life,
other than playing tennis

00:12:53.157 --> 00:12:56.516
which I, I stack up during
the course of a week

00:12:56.516 --> 00:12:58.426
quite a lot of, if I can,

00:12:58.426 --> 00:13:01.969
and, you know, get to set,
depending on your call time,

00:13:01.969 --> 00:13:04.519
and very often it's very early.

00:13:04.519 --> 00:13:06.102
And then you try to

00:13:07.021 --> 00:13:09.872
be there and be alert,
and awake, and alive,

00:13:09.872 --> 00:13:12.775
and ready to go every hour of the day.

00:13:12.775 --> 00:13:16.118
And if you work 12 hours
then you have to be

00:13:16.118 --> 00:13:19.115
alert every one of those hours.

00:13:19.115 --> 00:13:22.494
It's an important thing to stay focused.

00:13:22.494 --> 00:13:23.839
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:13:23.839 --> 00:13:26.614
I hope you enjoyed, I'd love
to know what did you take

00:13:26.614 --> 00:13:29.387
from this video that you
are going to immediately now

00:13:29.387 --> 00:13:32.018
apply to your life or
your business somehow,

00:13:32.018 --> 00:13:33.591
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:13:33.591 --> 00:13:34.944
I'm really curious to find out.

00:13:34.944 --> 00:13:36.827
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Derrick Cui,

00:13:36.827 --> 00:13:39.358
hope I pronounced that okay,
Derrick thank you so much

00:13:39.358 --> 00:13:41.788
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word,

00:13:41.788 --> 00:13:43.976
I really, really, really
appreciate the support, man,

00:13:43.976 --> 00:13:45.918
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:13:45.918 --> 00:13:47.554
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:13:47.554 --> 00:13:50.386
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:13:50.386 --> 00:13:54.553
and whatever your one word is,
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.586
(whooshing)

